<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>FutureOfWork on behaviorengineering.ai</title><link>https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-8/tags/futureofwork/</link><description>Recent content in FutureOfWork on behaviorengineering.ai</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 01:00:00 +1100</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-8/tags/futureofwork/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Follow your dreams</title><link>https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-8/cognitive-memetics/cows/2026-08-05-cow-w24/</link><pubDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 01:00:00 +1100</pubDate><guid>https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-8/cognitive-memetics/cows/2026-08-05-cow-w24/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Worrying hours are 24/7</title><link>https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-8/cognitive-memetics/cows/2026-07-22-cow-w22/</link><pubDate>Wed, 22 Jul 2026 01:00:00 +1100</pubDate><guid>https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-8/cognitive-memetics/cows/2026-07-22-cow-w22/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Location-agnostic stress</title><link>https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-8/cognitive-memetics/cows/2026-06-17-cow-w17/</link><pubDate>Wed, 17 Jun 2026 01:00:00 +1100</pubDate><guid>https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-8/cognitive-memetics/cows/2026-06-17-cow-w17/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Commute for the culture</title><link>https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-8/cognitive-memetics/cows/2026-05-07-cow-w11/</link><pubDate>Thu, 07 May 2026 01:00:00 +1100</pubDate><guid>https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-8/cognitive-memetics/cows/2026-05-07-cow-w11/</guid><description/></item><item><title>🤖 Will AI replace you? The uncomfortable truth about work</title><link>https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-8/mind-infrastructure/2026-04-26-will-ai-replace-me/</link><pubDate>Sun, 26 Apr 2026 01:00:00 +1100</pubDate><guid>https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-8/mind-infrastructure/2026-04-26-will-ai-replace-me/</guid><description>&lt;h3 id="the-leverage-shift"&gt;The leverage shift&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The real risk is the colleague, vendor, or new hire who produces acceptable work &lt;strong&gt;faster and cheaper&lt;/strong&gt; by treating models as leverage while others defend process for its own sake.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What matters is &lt;strong&gt;comparative advantage&lt;/strong&gt; in a world where mechanical cognition is partially commoditized. Debating whether AI is &amp;ldquo;truly&amp;rdquo; thinking is a distraction from the immediate economic shift.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="the-spell-check-mirror"&gt;The spell-check mirror&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The video uses spell-check as a historical mirror: it removed the prestige of memorizing exceptions and pushed the creative job up a layer. Ideas, structure, taste, and persuasion now matter more than catching every doubled letter.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>